t(19, 715, """Many people in our time toil and exhaust themselves to own a building or an apartment! The same goes for owning a car, the same for securing a lot of money to educate the children so they become cogs in the system of the 1945 world, the same for securing a sum in the bank, and for many worldly reasons!

Personally, I did none of all this

If owning a house or a car or educating children will be = the toil of years and the exhaustion of a lifetime that afflicted many people with diseases, and crushed them so they could not worship their Lord as He deserves, and they wasted their lives for the sake of this world, then wretched is the toil, wretched the exhaustion, and wretched the striving!

Any toil and any exhaustion that makes a person stand before his collapsed house and say: "The 'hardship' of my life is lost" is toil and exhaustion that truly expresses the misery of a lifetime, that is, an unbalanced life, either:
🔴 Health of body and health of self that were lost!
🔴 Worship that was not as it should be!!
🔴 A mind distracted from Allah the Most High!!!

Because misery is a word with what is in it and what is behind it; it is not random, and they do not say it by chance. It expresses a very early orientation in the mind, and in the system of the collective mind, to regard the house of this world as more important than excellence in worship, more important than the ease of the human self, and more important than the health of the body!

"The 'hardship' of my life is lost" is not merely the cry of one pained over the walls of an apartment, but a regrettable expression of the state humans have reached, from the Philippines in the east to Los Angeles in the west!

The human who has come to spend his whole life .. not a year or two .. but his whole life, for the sake of:

An apartment!!""")

h(19, 2200, """20 years abroad, for an owned apartment in a building not up to specifications and an eviction order; another's building was bombed, and a third's was flattened by an earthquake""")

t(20, 345, """When Allah the Great blesses you with the blessing of breaking and crumbling you, you first chase the causes thinking they will help, so He breaks you and crumbles you more, to make you see with your own eyes that the causes had no value in the journey of subjugation decreed before you were created. Then your mind awakens to the saying of the Great Lord: {All power belongs to Allah}, an awakening not merely to the word and meaning, but one flooded by the value of Allah's power. When the value floods you, you as a created being are crushed, crumble and melt, and you never again see your ego or your self until you die, and you live realizing very well that everything possible is not possible through you, and that everything probable, awaited and hoped for, you form nothing in the course of its happening but absolute nothingness!""")

h(20, 1100, """The Great Lord does not subdue you to humiliate you, but to unleash in you the greatest power of all!""")

t(20, 1840, """Then learn what our Lord loves and what He does not love. And beware of deluding yourself that Allah the Great loves what you love and dislikes what you dislike, for this absurdity is widespread!!""")

h(20, 2300, """You will not arrive except by this. Period. End of talk. Weigh every word and deed, every day! Every day! With the greatest scale: Allah loves this. Allah does not love this.""")

t(21, 505, """Ruined is the one for whom the "gatherings of nothing", the "deeds of nothing" and the "sayings of nothing" in his daily life rank higher than his private moments with his Lord.

Ruined .. his self is lowly .. his self is foolish .. he built the world he decided to live in and classified it as beneficial to his Hereafter and his worldly life, but in reality his classification was wrong, and he thought he was doing good work!""")

h(21, 1000, """How much people love wasting lives on what does not benefit, and what does the gravest harm in this world and the Hereafter!""")

t(21, 1840, """What you were forbidden is not part of the lawful that was made lawful to you. People become helpless when they do not restrain themselves from the desire for play and amusement, and for indulging with those who indulge, and from their passion for much gossip and much wasting of time; so they leave what is theirs and overstep into what is not theirs, that is, what was made unlawful for them and forbidden to them, and today it has become almost beyond counting:
🔴 Backbiting
🔴 Spreading tales
🔴 Inciting between a father and his children
🔴 Inciting between a mother and her daughters
🔴 Works of sorcery
🔴 Cutting off livelihoods
🔴 Indecencies and spreading them
🔴 Ingratitude to the spouse
🔴 Wronging the two weak ones, the child and the woman
🔴 Consuming wealth unjustly
🔴 Fathers' and mothers' undutifulness to their children
🔴 Children's undutifulness to their parents
🔴 Mutual hatred, belittling the truth and raging for the ego
🔴 Depriving a child of his father or mother after divorce""")

t(22, 60, """🔴 False testimony
🔴 Domineering in the name of religion, while religion is innocent of it
🔴 Accusing the righteous with falsehood and lies
🔴 Hurting souls, even with a look or a whisper

Then on the Day of Resurrection they come with mountains of stinking deeds and ugly acts and words, and say: We were only indulging and playing. Whoever wants it, let him take it: a scorching Fire whose stones demand more, never quenched by hunger or thirst, saying morning and evening: Are there more bodies of these wretched ones?!""")

h(22, 850, """Among the meanings of taking the Book with strength: that you take what is yours and leave what is not yours, for all that is lawful is yours""")

t(22, 1545, """{So hold fast to what has been revealed to you; indeed, you are on a straight path}
{And We wrote for him on the tablets an admonition of everything and a detailed explanation of all things: So take them with strength and command your people to take the best of them}.""")

h(22, 2100, """The greatest meaning of victory over the self: that you take the Book with strength""")

t(23, 205, """{O Yahya, take the Book with strength. And We gave him wisdom while yet a child}""")

h(23, 650, """Your worth with your Great Lord: when your self comes to you, you say: My Lord does not love this, so you do not do it, and you turn away strong, lofty and guided!""")

t(23, 1370, """Because you were created, and you are capable, created with the real capabilities in you to do that.

Our Great Lord, holy are His names and attributes, says: {He has succeeded who purifies it, and he has failed who buries it}
And our Great Lord, the King, the Mighty, the Wise, holy in the heavens and the earth and exalted with a great exaltation, says:
{And all of them will come to Him on the Day of Resurrection alone}""")

h(23, 2000, """The heart is a vessel and a leader: a vessel for the fitrah, a leader for the self. Return it to this fitrah of its; it is your responsibility and no one will help you in it""")

h(24, 550, """Your self is the course of one of two paths. Your heart holds your guidance! Your heart directs your path; your self resists the director""")

h(24, 1700, """What kills the bond with Allah the Great, our Lord, is the self that said: Allah loved me, so He made my owner rich!""")

t(24, 2400, """How great is a moment of illness if it surprises you and a light descends into your heart with it! Do you know when? When you humble yourself on earth with true humility .. 100%""")

h(25, 450, """What kills the bond with Allah the Great, our Lord, is the self that said: Who is mightier than me in strength!""")

h(25, 1600, """Its arrogance is its owner's ruin. Nothing keeps people from guidance but the arrogance of their selves!""")

t(25, 2195, """Orders of injustice issue from it every day.

The order does not issue from the mind (the heart), nor from the spirit, nor from the body. The order issues from the self.

This is what destroyed the misguided before us, and destroys today those living in our time, and will destroy peoples coming after us. This destroyer, then destroyed, is the one that issues the order of injustice every day, and its owner sets off like a blind man, like a fool, like one who has lost his mind, carrying out what it demands, while it sits enthroned on a great throne, clad in the garment of tyranny, the garment of subjugating the children of humanity, the garment of evil, the garment of aggression, the garment of its own ruin. It makes others weep, crushes others' souls, and does dreadful things on earth; then when it goes to Hell, it says: My Lord, send me back!""")

h(26, 500, """The self is a vessel with no bottom and no end! Clad in the garment of sins upon the throne of falsehood!""")

t(26, 1160, """In you is a self that seeks falsehood and desires.. Built into it is the heart by which the self is set straight, so the self holds both its disease and its cure! When its diseases grow severe, its antidote is from it and within it: a heart dwelling in it, created as part of it. In it is the cure, in it the solution, and in it salvation. But it does not work well unless the self's owner imprisons it with his own hands and locks it in; then the reward descends from heaven for the heart to work. Did you think the heart works on an earthly energy? Far from it, far from it! The heart by which a human is set right works only on a great, heavenly, luminous energy, and this great energy does not descend into the heart unless its owner first imprisons the self; this is the condition, without which the heart will not work .. Because the heart's working is a reward for imprisoning the self, since our role on earth is to imprison the self, not to give it the key. If a human gives his self the key to his Hereafter, he loses the light in the heart, and his bond with Allah the Most High is cut, even if he prays, fasts, performs Hajj and Umrah, and gives zakat.""")

h(26, 2000, """The conscience pump in your self is your self's fiercest enemy! The self is your enemy, and within it is its enemy!""")

t(27, 135, """In you is the miracle of Allah the Great in creating your heart: a lump of flesh that pumps blood, and without pumping blood your body dies and you give up the spirit!

And it is a lump of flesh that pumps conscience, by which the true human becomes aware, and by which a human is able to reflect and reason, because it is the true mind. Without your using it properly, religion dies, and the spirit dies of grief and pain.

And the conscience pump works only by imprisoning the self in the castle's dungeon!""")

h(27, 900, """Your components: a body that strives, a spirit that moves the body, a heart that grasps the truth, a self that seeks falsehood""")

t(27, 1640, """Your conscience, your religion, your tawhid and your nearness to Allah the Great are all a castle. This castle has a great gate, and in the castle is a dungeon, and the right place of the self is always to be inside the dungeon. So what is your state if the key of the castle is in the hand of the self, instead of its place being the dungeon? It will open the gate to the qarin (the companion devil) to harm you with every kind of harm: continuous whispers, demanding that you do every bad thing, and possession.""")

h(27, 2200, """The whispers of the qarin become noticeable when the Muslim's self has betrayed him and let the qarin in upon him""")

t(28, 390, """Your self is your weakness, because it does not work for you, and to it you are cheaper than an onion skin. You are one thing and it is another. Your enemy is within you and you do not know!

Your enemy is awake inside you, watching you, and you do not know it exists! All your self cares about is pleasures that lead you to the Fire, because it loves desires so intensely that the torment of the Fire does not deter it, and so nothing deters it except for those who seek Allah's help. Even if you sat a thousand years reminding it of the torment of the Fire, it would respond, then slip away; it is disciplined only by the power of a divine light that makes it retreat and collapse. And the power of the divine light in your heart is a divine gift given only to those who strive in the love of Allah; their hearts fill with light, so the self in them weakens greatly, and when the self in them weakens, the power of the qarin recedes greatly.""")

h(28, 1200, """Your self and the qarin are friends for life. Do you still trust it? It is your weakness and your heart is your strength; in your heart is your will""")

h(28, 2200, """Your self never loves you. Your self loves itself, not you""")

h(29, 900, """If you reform the self, the qarin slinks away greatly. The self has its demands and the qarin has his plans, and the qarin uses the self because it is his way in""")

h(29, 2000, """If you do not know, as daily conduct and not as words, that you are in a battle with the self, then you are a Muslim, but your path is not the path of the Prophet ﷺ""")

t(30, 170, """Your wronging yourself prevents you from reaching Allah the Great, our Lord, holy are His names and attributes, great in the heavens and the earth, and exalted with a great exaltation""")

h(30, 700, """The balance of the battle with the self: bringing injustice to the self and to people down to zero""")

h(30, 1800, """Allah the Great, our Lord, is known only through the fierceness of the battle with the self""")

t(30, 2445, """How do we know?
🟢 When the matter is definitely for reform on earth, by helping a person or bringing happiness to a person with what holds the good of the Hereafter and this world, without strife and without private or public harm!""")

t(31, 60, """🟢 And when you are pushed toward the matter illogically, in a way that runs counter to the logic of things, in a manner that, if you measured it against the logic of people's minds, behaviors and customs, you would find the face of your conduct and their conduct completely contrary to people's customs of thinking and logic and to what people are used to!

Then this destiny is either an order of action from Allah the Most High for you to do it and carry it out with a sincere, pure intention of obedience to Allah, or a test of submission to Allah the Most High and His command: will you submit or not submit to Allah the Most High, and to what Allah the Most High pushes you toward, through clear, evident messages that you must understand with the understanding of the knowers of Allah?!

So in both cases the matter is between a test of execution and a test of surrender!

If you seek your Lord's guidance (istikhara) about a good deed clearly good for a person, with no ambiguity that it is good for a person, and you find your self holding you back, uninterested and unwilling, yet Allah the Most High pushes you and sends you illogical signs one after another, which you know and understand and grasp with the awareness of a perceptive person as illogical according to human minds and their limited understandings, but in the understanding of the knowers of Allah they came illogical by human logic to draw their attention to the fact that they came thus, so that the knowers can classify them with awareness and confidence as overpowering divine messages; then they know they must be carried out, and are not optional!

An example is your seeing a weak person in a street who wants to cross it and no one helps him, but every time you approach to help him he curses and insults you, while logic says he should thank you, yet cars nearly kill him and run him over. Every time he insults you, your self is disgusted with him and you say: I will not help him, but your conscience pushes you hard to help him, and every time you approach him again he curses and insults you. This is contrary to reason and logic. So do not think then that you were brought and dragged to the place, at an hour of the hours, a minute of the minutes, and on a specific day of the days, to look at him and leave him because he cursed you and acted irrationally with you. The irrational is the deepest and greatest proof that you are charged with this weak man to get him across the street, and that the matter is not your choice. Had he smiled at you, praised you and thanked you, the matter would have been weaker in the degree of your being charged with it; but since he insulted you, know that you are being tested in him, you are being examined, and your exam takes place in him. So take the matter with strength, and obey your Master.""")

h(31, 1700, """Many destinies are commands from our Great Lord""")

t(31, 2265, """And you will not know your self until you dismantle the make-up you were created upon! And you will not dismantle the make-up you were created with until you understand who you are and what you are made of. As long as you think you are one thing, you will understand nothing! You are 3 things! A body that has no relation to the ongoing struggle, a self that commands evil, and a spirit that suffers because it represents the conscience.

The explanation is in a recording today, Allah the Most High willing.""")

h(32, 400, """You will not know Allah the Great if you do not know your self!""")

h(32, 1500, """Your self conspires against you with the qarin! It befriends him and he befriends it! It loves him and he loves it!""")

h(33, 250, """Your self is a driller of the ship of your solitude with Allah! When it calms down, the drilling stops!""")

h(33, 1100, """The ship of the believers may be holed every day, and the ship of the knowers of Allah may be holed every month!""")

t(33, 1865, """If Allah grants victory to the believers in people's future, it will be as though they had become rich and become free of need to commit anything that angers Allah the Great, because Allah's wealth on earth is strength and impregnability. Being made free of need by Allah's wealth is, for the believers, a Muhammadan and Solomonic Sunnah, where the freedom from need is not from people, because Allah the Great, our Lord, commanded us to live life loving one another and doing good to one another, so none of us can do without the presence of people in his life. But for the believers, being free of need through Allah's wealth comes by harnessing the wealth of Allah that He pours upon them, and this is of course not our present era nor our time; rather the talk is about a world other than this world of ours. Then the "believing" rich become free of need through wealth so that it raises their manners and their good morals, and lifts from their breasts what may still cling there of the share of this world that drives to error, not the share of this world that Allah the Most High made lawful. Their morals become multiplied and their manners multiplied, and by these multiplied multiples they reform more on earth. For if a human was a believer when his Lord enriched him, then lived in a system of faith and piety and a society disciplined by laws, its good and its bad, then stronger horizons open in the self of this believer whom Allah enriched from His wealth, so that he sets for society a higher and better example in goodness of self. And by the wealth of Allah the Most High many of his behaviors are zeroed out, those caused by lack of money, such as family problems, so he can then retain with kindness or release with goodness. If a trade of his loses, he does not grieve; if his wealth increases, he does not transgress; if he falls ill, he is patient; if he is blessed, he gives thanks with the thanks of those who act, not the thanks of the tongue; and if the demands of his self grow intense, he meets them with the lawful, so that they do not hole the ship of his worship and his solitude with his Lord. For the self is like a driller that leaves no spot in the ship of a human's salvation without holing it, without hesitation and without stopping! So with Allah's wealth in the future, Allah willing, if only we would all return to these words; perhaps they will make it easier to keep the ship from being holed.""")

h(34, 500, """Freedom from need is manners and morals, because it is used for reform on earth!""")

t(34, 1205, """Do not fill the world with arrogance, tyranny and shouting; all of this moves you nowhere! What moves you is calm, deliberation and wisdom.

And do not think that those who do not understand life's realities will achieve what they aim for by much shouting, for I have seen the kinds of these people: among them the scowler, the pompous talker, the inflamed, the arrogant, and the overflowing!

And you will not find among them or in them a single one with a sharp, seasoned mind!""")

h(34, 2000, """The confident step is not in stamping the feet hard on the ground!""")

t(35, 125, """An incorrect sentence .. What is built over years does not collapse in a moment .. It was never built in the first place, but the parties to the human relationship (family - social) imagined they had built it!""")

h(35, 600, """Relationships are built over years and collapse in a moment""")

t(35, 1335, """And people in enmity are between the way of fearing Allah and the way of forgetting Allah""")

h(35, 1800, """When you stab a body you make a slain man, and when you stab a soul you make an enemy""")

h(36, 400, """Lions do not become lions by applause, but by the amount of blood that was shed!""")

t(36, 1055, """A father and mother who did not raise them, or souls that upbringing does not set straight and discipline does not benefit, and only the stick is their cure?""")

h(36, 1500, """Lack of manners has reached holding the marriage contract in the mosque, with touching hands and embracing in the House of Allah!""")

t(36, 2225, """I ask Allah the Great, our Lord, the Most Merciful, the All-Powerful, the Able, to heal you, O Eisa.

Due to his being afflicted with a rare and very complex genetic mutation that affected his immune and nervous systems, this rare medical condition caused breakdown and severe shedding in the skin layers of the child Eisa.""")
